Moonlight OS has its own list of commands that are built into the system. ##Here you can see them

  1. moonutils is a command to launch a built in task manager, that displays realtime processes and errors. 
  2. why is a command that shows you the reason why a specific task is waiting/crashed, it also mentions recent mentions of the process in the system
  3. recent is a command that shows you the most recent error in the system, it also tells you the reason of the error

The command list will be updating as the OS will update
